capability text/find-first  where a text first holds another
  heroes  strings.index_of
  go      strings.Index, strings.IndexByte, strings.IndexRune
  rust    str::find (a text, a character)
  python  str.find, str.index
  note    absent is `not_found`, where Go and Python's find answer -1; the empty text is found at 0, as all three say. A failure's message, of this and of every function of the package that fails, quotes a text of 32 bytes or fewer escaped as Python's `repr` writes it (a double quote always the one escaped; a control, a format character, a line or paragraph separator, a space but U+0020, a private or unassigned code point as `\x`, `\u` or `\U` and its digits) and names a longer one by its length, the bound `bytes` puts on its own. Measured 2026-11-19 over every function that fails, on a million-byte input and a 5,000-byte needle: the longest message 128 bytes (`quote_windows_args`'s), where until that day `quote_windows_args` wrote 1,000,090 bytes for a 1,000,001-byte program name, an escape and a line feed reached raw all 19 messages that named a short input holding them, two bounds stood (40 and 32 bytes), two wordings ("from byte N" and "at or after byte N", now the second everywhere), and a long needle read "no a text of 5000 bytes in" (now "no text of 5000 bytes in"); tests hold each

